Codegen limitation: ta.crossover/crossunder requires inline expression arguments

Parse: ✅ (AST generation successful)
Generate: ❌ (Error: ta.crossover requires CallExpression arguments for inline generation)
Compile: ❌ (Cannot proceed due to codegen failure)
Execute: ❌ (Cannot proceed due to compilation failure)

The ta.crossover() and ta.crossunder() functions in the codegen require their arguments
to be simple expressions, but when variables (tenkanSen, kijunSen) are passed, the inline
generation fails. This needs codegen enhancement to handle variable references in cross
functions.

Temporary workaround: Store previous values and manually implement crossover logic:
  longCross = tenkanSen > kijunSen and tenkanSen[1] <= kijunSen[1]
